# Trivy IaC Security Scan - Accepted Risks
# ==========================================
# Each entry documents why a finding is accepted rather than fixed.
# Review periodically and remove entries when underlying configs are hardened.

# --- Public subnets (by design) ---
# Public subnets require map_public_ip_on_launch=true for NAT gateways,
# load balancers, and bastion hosts. Private subnets do NOT have this set.
AVD-AWS-0164

# --- Egress rules (by design) ---
# EKS nodes and VPC endpoints require outbound internet access for:
# - Container image pulls (ECR, DockerHub, GCR)
# - AWS API calls, CloudWatch logging, Kubernetes API
# - Helm chart downloads, OS package updates
# Restricting egress to specific IPs would break Kubernetes functionality.
AVD-AWS-0104

# --- IAM wildcarded resources (by design) ---
# Cluster Autoscaler and Karpenter require broad EC2/ASG permissions to
# discover and manage nodes across all ASGs/node pools. This is the
# standard IAM policy recommended by the upstream projects.
# VPC Flow Logs require CloudWatch Logs access across log groups.
# See: https://github.com/kubernetes/autoscaler/blob/master/cluster-autoscaler/cloudprovider/aws/README.md
# See: https://karpenter.sh/docs/getting-started/migrating-from-cas/
AVD-AWS-0057

# --- GCP IAP SSH firewall (by design) ---
# 35.235.240.0/20 is Google's Identity-Aware Proxy range, not arbitrary
# public internet. IAP provides authenticated, audited SSH access.
# See: https://cloud.google.com/iap/docs/using-tcp-forwarding
AVD-GCP-0027

# --- GKE Autopilot legacy metadata endpoints ---
# GKE Autopilot manages node configuration including metadata endpoints.
# The cluster resource itself doesn't expose a metadata config block;
# Google disables legacy endpoints on Autopilot by default.
AVD-GCP-0048

# --- GKE master authorized networks ---
# Dev/staging clusters intentionally allow broad access for development.
# Production clusters should enable master authorized networks (tracked
# separately in the infrastructure hardening backlog).
AVD-GCP-0061

# --- EKS public cluster access (variable-controlled) ---
# var.cluster_endpoint_public_access defaults to true for dev/staging
# to allow kubectl access without VPN. Production environments should
# set this to false (enforced via tfvars, not module defaults).
AVD-AWS-0040

# --- EKS public access CIDRs (variable-controlled) ---
# var.cluster_endpoint_public_access_cidrs is configurable per environment.
# Dev uses 0.0.0.0/0 for convenience; production restricts to VPN CIDRs.
AVD-AWS-0041

# --- S3 bucket encryption ---
# State bucket uses AES256 (SSE-S3) which is encrypted at rest.
# Trivy flags this because it's not using a customer-managed KMS key (CMK).
# SSE-S3 is acceptable for Terraform state; CMK adds key rotation complexity
# without meaningful security benefit for this use case.
AVD-AWS-0088
AVD-AWS-0132

# --- CloudSQL TLS (variable-controlled) ---
# var.ssl_mode is configurable per environment. Dev allows non-TLS for
# local testing; staging/production should enforce TLS via tfvars.
AVD-GCP-0015

# --- ElastiCache encryption (variable-controlled) ---
# var.at_rest_encryption_enabled and var.transit_encryption_enabled are
# configurable per environment. Dev may disable for performance testing;
# production should enable both (enforced via tfvars).
AVD-AWS-0045
AVD-AWS-0051
